# Environment variables for the DQ Rebranding site.
#
# This file is committed on purpose. Real values are never committed.
#
# Status: this project currently requires NO environment variables.
# `npm run build` and `npm run dev` work on a clean clone with no .env file,
# because every page is statically prerendered and nothing calls a private API
# at build time or at runtime. Verified: the codebase contains no `process.env`
# reference.

# How to add a variable, when the day comes:
#
# 1. Add it below, with a placeholder value and one line saying what it is for
#    and whether it is needed at build time or runtime.
# 2. Create `.env.local` on your machine and put the real value there.
#    `.env*` is gitignored, so it cannot be committed by accident.
# 3. Set the real value in Netlify under Site configuration, Environment
#    variables. Build-time variables must be set before the deploy that needs
#    them.
# 4. Never put a real key in a commit message, a PR description, a screenshot,
#    or a document in this repo. If one leaks, rotate it first, then clean up.

# EXAMPLE_NAME=
